    "https://ffd.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fairfield-CT/Instructor-for-Microsoft-Excel-Lab-Sessions_JR0003415": {
      "title": "Instructor for Microsoft Excel Lab Sessions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description: Dolan School of Business, Fairfield University, invites applications for an instructor of Microsoft Excel lab sessions starting Fall 2026 semester. The instructor will provide in-class Microsoft Excel training for business students taking DATA 1101 (Business Analytics) during the following hours: Wednesday      9:30-11:30AM and 12:30-2:30PM Thursday           9:30-11:30AM and 12:30-2:30PM Candidates must have a strong commitment to teaching, innovation, and excellence in using technology in the classroom. Candidates with demonstrated proficiency in programming, data science, and data visualization are especially encouraged to apply. This position will help prepare students to pass Microsoft Excel evaluation. Requirements: Candidates must have a Master’s Degree in Business Analytics, Data Science, Computer Science, or a related field. Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  Only complete applications will be reviewed by the search committee.  For full consideration, the following materials are required: Curriculum vitae Letter of application Statement of teaching philosophy Fairfield University, founded in 1942, is an independent Jesuit Catholic university with an active, collegial, and pluralistic faculty.  We are located on the Connecticut coast about an hour from New York City and thirty minutes from New Haven.  The Dolan School of Business is AACSB International accredited and ranked among Bloomberg Business Week’s and US News & World Report’s best business schools.  Category: Academic - Adjunct Faculty Performs such other duties, responsibilities, and activities as required by supervisor and as departmental/University needs indicate.    *Disclaimer The above information indicates the general nature and level of work performed by employees within this classification. It is not designed 